###Step 1: Finding the length $BC$



[[☃ image 1]]

$\begin{align} 
BC^2&= {\redE{8}^2 +\redE{5}^2 }  &&\text{Pythagorean theorem}
\\\\
BC&= \sqrt{\redE{8}^2 +\redE{5}^2 }  &&\text{Square root both sides}
\\\\
&=\tealE{\sqrt{89}}
\end{align}$

We're looking for an approximate answer, so we won't try to simplify this radical. Also, let's not round until the end.

###Step 2: Finding the length $CD$



[[☃ image 1]]

$\begin{align} 
CD^2&= \redE{4}^2 +\redE{4}^2  &&\text{Pythagorean theorem}
\\\\
CD&= \sqrt{\redE{4}^2 +\redE{4}^2 } &&\text{Square root both sides}
\\\\
&=\goldE{\sqrt{32}}
\end{align}$

We're looking for an approximate answer, so we won't try to simplify this radical. Also, let's not round until the end.
